<title>USA: PG&amp;E Diablo Canyon 1 at full output today.</title>
<headline>PG&amp;E Diablo Canyon 1 at full output today.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pacific Gas &amp; Electric Co (PG&amp;E) said Monday the 1,087 megawatt (MW) unit 1 at the Diablo Canyon nuclear generating facility was expected to resume full operation today.</p>
<p>The Avila Beach, Calif., unit was producing at 97 percent power, and was planned to achieve full output this morning.</p>
<p>Diablo Canyon unit 1 tripped off line Nov 22 after a fire in an auxiliary power grounding transformer.</p>
<p>The neighboring Diablo Canyon unit 2, rated at 1,073 MW, was producing at 100 percent capacity, PG&amp;E said.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk 212-859-1622</p>
</text>
